# Security headers for every page and file served from the site's static
# assets on Cloudflare. Responses the Worker builds itself (/api/contact) don't
# pass through this file. The build adds an immutable Cache-Control rule for
# /_astro/* to the copy it deploys.
#
# - nosniff: browsers must not guess a file's type, so a file can't be run as
#   a script it isn't.
# - Referrer-Policy: other sites see our domain, not full page addresses.
# - X-Frame-Options / frame-ancestors: only our own pages may show ours in a
#   frame, which protects the contact form from clickjacking (two forms, for
#   older and newer browsers).
# - Permissions-Policy: turns off device features the site never uses. It
#   doesn't touch what the YouTube embed is allowed (autoplay, fullscreen...).
# - Strict-Transport-Security: browsers always use HTTPS for www for a year.
#   A header sent from www can only ever cover www (and hosts under it), never
#   the apex or mail hosts; the apex doesn't get it at all, since Cloudflare's
#   redirect rule answers there before the Worker runs.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
